    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter July 3rd with a clear offensive blueprint, led by the elite pairing of **Yordan Alvarez** (86.62) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13). **Yordan Alvarez** is in a tier of his own today against N. Martinez, benefiting from a massive +18% bump due to the favorable 4.72 xERA of the opposing starter and an elite 0.477 xwOBA projection. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** anchors our pursuit of the scarce stolen base category; his matchup against Pallante is opportunistic, as the starter\u2019s slow delivery significantly boosts **Pete Crow-Armstrong**\u2019s stolen base probability, pushing his efficiency score well into the elite range. Joining them in the top tier is **Christian Yelich** (74.33), who draws a prime matchup against J. Cabrera. **Christian Yelich** receives a cumulative +23% boost from platoon advantages and a leadoff spot, making him a cornerstone of today's scoring potential.\n\nMid-tier value is anchored by **Junior Caminero** (74.38) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.20), both of whom are poised to outperform their base projections. **Junior Caminero** faces Arrighetti with a strong xwOBA profile, while **Casey Schmitt** sees a massive +19% boost from the opposing SP\u2019s 4.97 xERA and a favorable park factor, making him a surprisingly strong play at MI. We also find solid utility in **Carson Benge** (60.20) and **Nelson Velazquez** (59.43), both of whom remain above our 40-point floor despite some tactical caution. **Kazuma Okamoto** (52.85) and **Caleb Durbin** (48.56) round out the lineup; while they face tougher arms in L. Castillo and Detmers respectively, their roles in the middle of the order keep them in the starting rotation for today's slate.\n\nThe most difficult decision of the morning involved **Luke Raley** (39.07), who narrowly missed the starting lineup by less than a full point. While **Luke Raley** maintains a decent platoon advantage, the matchup against the elite Cease\u2014whose low 3.01 xERA acted as a significant anchor on the projection\u2014forced him below our 40-point strict efficiency floor. We are opting to bench **Luke Raley** alongside **Chase Meidroth** and **Jacob Gonzalez** to preserve our game caps against high-quality pitching. As a final reminder, monitor the status of **Rece Hinds**, who remains stashed in the minors; ensure all other bench assets like **Trea Turner**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Hyeseong Kim**, **Colt Keith**, **Zac Veen**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Luis Pena** are adjusted for any late-breaking weather or lineup changes.",
